WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.849
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "will you not stay with me for one night and be my messenger?

2
00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:15.929
The boy is so thirsty, and the mother so sad."

3
00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:19.723
"I don't think I like boys," answered the Swallow.

4
00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:29.420
"Last summer, when I was staying on the river, there were two rude boys, the miller's sons, who were always throwing stones at me.

5
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:39.391
They never hit me, of course; we swallows fly far too well for that, and besides, I come of a family famous for its agility.

6
00:00:39.392 --> 00:00:42.749
But still, it was a mark of disrespect."

7
00:00:42.749 --> 00:00:48.059
But the Happy Prince looked so sad that the little Swallow was sorry.

8
00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:55.915
"It is very cold here," he said, "but I will stay with you for one night and be your messenger."

9
00:00:55.916 --> 00:01:01.139
"Thank you, little Swallow," said the Prince.

10
00:01:01.139 --> 00:01:10.024
So the Swallow picked out the great ruby from the Prince's sword and flew away with it in his beak over the roofs of the town.

11
00:01:10.024 --> 00:01:16.077
He passed by the cathedral tower, where the white marble angels were sculptured.

12
00:01:16.077 --> 00:01:20.286
He passed by the palace and heard the sound of dancing.

13
00:01:20.286 --> 00:01:24.139
A beautiful girl came out on the balcony with her lover.

14
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:32.019
"How wonderful the stars are," he said to her, "and how wonderful is the power of love!"

15
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.819
"I hope my dress will be ready in time for the State Ball," she answered.

16
00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:43.877
"I have ordered passionflowers to be embroidered on it; but the seamstresses are so lazy."

17
00:01:43.878 --> 00:01:49.980
He passed over the river, and saw the lanterns hanging to the masts of the ships.

18
00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:58.361
He passed over the market, and saw the old men bargaining with each other and weighing out money in copper scales.

19
00:01:58.361 --> 00:02:03.353
At last, he came to the poor house and looked in.

20
00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:11.491
The boy was tossing feverishly on his bed, and the mother had fallen asleep, she was so tired.

21
00:02:11.491 --> 00:02:17.560
In he hopped, and laid the great ruby on the table beside the woman's thimble.

22
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:24.138
Then, he flew gently round the bed, fanning the boy's forehead with his wings.

23
00:02:24.138 --> 00:02:33.462
"How cool I feel," said the boy. "I must be getting better," and he sank into a delicious slumber.

24
00:02:33.462 --> 00:02:39.556
Then, the Swallow flew back to the Happy Prince and told him what he had done.

25
00:02:39.557 --> 00:02:47.014
"It is curious," he remarked, "but I feel quite warm now, although it is so cold."

26
00:02:47.014 --> 00:02:52.006
"That is because you have done a good action," said the Prince.

27
00:02:52.006 --> 00:02:57.890
And the little Swallow began to think, and then, he fell asleep.

28
00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.983
Thinking always made him sleepy.

29
00:03:00.984 --> 00:03:05.524
When day broke, he flew down to the river and had a bath.

30
00:03:05.524 --> 00:03:13.196
"What a remarkable phenomenon," said the Professor of Ornithology as he was passing over the bridge.

31
00:03:13.196 --> 00:03:18.948
"A swallow in winter!" And he wrote a long letter about it to the local newspaper.

32
00:03:18.948 --> 00:03:25.335
Everyone quoted it, it was full of so many words that they could not understand.

33
00:03:25.336 --> 00:03:32.390
"Tonight, I go to Egypt," said the Swallow, and he was in high spirits at the prospect.

34
00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:38.635
He visited all the public monuments and sat a long time on top of the church steeple.

35
00:03:38.636 --> 00:03:46.503
Wherever he went, the Sparrows chirruped, and said to each other, "What a distinguished stranger!"

36
00:03:46.527 --> 00:03:49.527
So he enjoyed himself very much.

37
00:03:49.527 --> 00:03:53.742
When the moon rose, he flew back to the Happy Prince.

38
00:03:53.742 --> 00:03:59.629
"Have you any commissions for Egypt?" he cried. "I am just starting."

39
00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:09.301
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "will you not stay with me one night longer?"

40
00:04:09.301 --> 00:04:13.602
"I am waited for in Egypt," answered the Swallow.

41
00:04:13.602 --> 00:04:18.941
"Tomorrow, my friends will fly up to our meeting place on the River Nile.

42
00:04:18.941 --> 00:04:26.533
The hippopotamus lies there among the cattails, and on a great granite throne sits the God Memnon.

43
00:04:26.533 --> 00:04:36.960
All night long, he watches the stars, and when the morning star shines, he utters one cry of joy, and then, he is silent.

44
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.677
At noon, the yellow lions come down to the water's edge to drink.

45
00:04:42.677 --> 00:04:49.765
They have eyes like green jewels, and their roar is louder than the roar of the river."

46
00:04:49.765 --> 00:05:01.824
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "far away across the city, I see a young man in a garret.

47
00:05:01.825 --> 00:05:11.897
He is leaning over a desk covered with papers, and in a glass by his side, there is a bunch of withered violets.

48
00:05:11.897 --> 00:05:21.933
His hair is brown and crisp, and his lips are red as a pomegranate, and he has large and dreamy eyes.

49
00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:30.675
He is trying to finish a play for the Director of the Theatre, but he is too cold to write any more.

50
00:05:30.675 --> 00:05:36.650
There is no fire in the fireplace, and hunger has made him faint."

51
00:05:36.659 --> 00:05:45.085
"I will wait with you one night longer," said the Swallow, who really had a good heart. "Shall I take him another ruby?"

52
00:05:45.085 --> 00:05:50.886
"Alas! I have no ruby now," said the Prince.

53
00:05:50.886 --> 00:05:54.159
"My eyes are all that I have left.

54
00:05:54.183 --> 00:06:02.810
They are made of rare sapphires, which were brought out of India a thousand years ago.

55
00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.507
Pluck out one of them and take it to him.

56
00:06:06.507 --> 00:06:13.290
He will sell it to the jeweler and buy food and firewood, and finish his play."

57
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:20.821
"Dear Prince," said the Swallow, "I cannot do that," and he began to weep.

58
00:06:20.821 --> 00:06:29.826
"Swallow, Swallow, little Swallow," said the Prince, "do as I command you."

59
00:06:29.826 --> 00:06:36.718
So the Swallow plucked out the Prince's eye and flew away to the student's garret.

60
00:06:36.718 --> 00:06:41.550
It was easy enough to get in, as there was a hole in the roof.

61
00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.138
Through this, he darted and came into the room.

62
00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:58.619
The young man had his head buried in his hands, so he did not hear the flutter of the bird's wings, and when he looked up, he found the beautiful sapphire lying on the withered violets.

63
00:06:58.619 --> 00:07:03.279
"I am beginning to be appreciated," he cried.

64
00:07:03.279 --> 00:07:12.181
"This is from some great admirer. Now I can finish my play," and he looked quite happy.

65
00:07:12.181 --> 00:07:16.371
The next day, the Swallow flew down to the harbor.

66
00:07:16.372 --> 00:07:24.193
He sat on the mast of a large vessel and watched the sailors hauling big chests out of the hold with ropes.

67
00:07:24.193 --> 00:07:29.583
"Heave a-hoy!" they shouted as each chest came up.

68
00:07:29.583 --> 00:07:39.316
"I am going to Egypt!" cried the Swallow, but nobody minded him, and when the moon rose, he flew back to the Happy Prince.

69
00:07:39.317 --> 00:07:43.583
"I am come to bid you good-bye," he cried.

